"""Walk-through of lesson 39, Design a News Feed.

Example numbers (mine, checked by script; they follow the section text): 200 million daily users x 10 opens = 2 billion feed loads a day = about 23,000 a second;
50 million posts a day = about 600 a second (40 reads per post); a user follows 200 accounts.
Pull: 23,000 x 200 = 4.6 million lookups a second; if a lookup is slow 1% of the time, 1 - 0.99^200 = 87% of loads hit one.
Push: 600 x 200 = 120,000 cache writes a second. Ids only: 200 million lists x 800 ids x 8 bytes = 1.28 TB.
Celebrity: 50 million followers at 100,000 writes a second = 500 s, over 8 minutes. Idle users: 1,000 of 3,000 followers active (a third).
Cache wiped: 200 million users back within an hour = 55,556 rebuilds a second x 200 lookups = 11.1 million lookups a second, 2.4x the pull model; cap 5,000 a second.
"""
